        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is Initial Display Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1775453271917",
            "false": "1778111033846"
          },
          "code": "IF_INITDISPLAY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1778111907600",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778111907600_condition",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.appFlow === \"InitDisplay\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Master Risks Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "MASTER_RISKS_WIDGET",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775506944179",
          "id": "1775453271917",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775453271919_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Instructions\nUse a multiRecordWidget with cols \"Type\", \"Severity\", and \"Total Requisition Lines\".\nWidget title should be \"Risk summary\".\nThe multiRecordWidget must have exactly 3 rows.\nDo not sort by severity, count, total, or any dynamic value.\nRender rows in this exact order:\n1. Possible purchase splitting\n2. High-value line with vague description\n3. Unusually high amounts for category\nThe widget description: **MUST** leave it empty.\n\n### Column Mapping\nType: Use the value of \"description\" in the provided data.\n\nSeverity: Build the Severity cell as an exact badge object, not a string.\n- If the row severity is \"High\", use exactly { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"High\", \"priority\": \"alert\" }.\n- If the row severity is \"Medium\", use exactly { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"Medium\", \"priority\": \"warning\" }.\n- Never use priority \"warning\" for severity \"High\".\n- Never use priority \"medium\" for severity \"Medium\".\n- Do not infer badge priority from the text label; use only the exact mapping above.\n\nTotal Requisition Lines: Use the value of \"total\" in the provided data.\n\n### Badge Cell Examples\nHigh severity cells example: [\"Possible purchase splitting\", { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"High\", \"priority\": \"alert\" }, 7]\nMedium severity cells example: [\"Unusually high amounts for category\", { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"Medium\", \"priority\": \"warning\" }, 11]\n\n### Drilldown Navigation Rules\nFor each row, evaluate that row's provided data total as a number.\n- If total is greater than 0, include that row's drillDownAction using the command specified for that risk below.\n- If total is 0, negative, missing, null, blank, or not numeric, omit drillDownAction entirely from that row.\n- Do not replace drillDownAction with an empty string, disabled command, placeholder command, no-op command, or any other fallback command.\n\n### Data\nThe following data entries define the fixed table row positions. Always render them in this order, even when totals or severities differ.\n\nFor 1st row: {{$context.$variables.splitPurchaseRisk_baseWidgetData}}\nThis row is Possible purchase splitting.\nUse drillDownAction only when this row's total is greater than 0, with command: ora.Invoke(\"navigateToSplitReqRiskItemFocus\", { \"payload\": <payload attribute from data provided> }).\n\nFor 2nd row: {{$context.$variables.highValueVagueDescRiskWidgetData}}\nThis row is High-value line with vague description.\nUse drillDownAction only when this row's total is greater than 0, with command: ora.Invoke(\"navigateToHighValueVagueDescRiskItemFocus\", { \"payload\": <payload attribute from data provided> }).\n\nFor 3rd row: {{$context.$variables.highCategoryAmountRiskWidgetData}}\nThis row is Unusually high amounts for category.\nUse drillDownAction only when this row's total is greater than 0, with command: ora.Invoke(\"navigateToUnusuallyHighAmountsForCategoryRiskItemFocus\", { \"payload\": <payload attribute from data provided> }).\n\nIf the data provided is missing or incomplete, go ahead and generate a multiRecordWidget with the data you do have in the fixed row order above, and still apply the drilldown navigation rules above.\n\n## OUTPUT REQUIREMENT\nProduce the multiRecordWidget and nothing else.\n**MUST NOT** generate or include any insights text in the output."
            },
            {
              "id": "1775453271917_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1778111033846",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778111033846_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Given the following info generate a summary, never mention Ids:\n\nIf total is 0, it means there is actually no risk.\n\nSplit risk: {{$context.$variables.splitPurchaseRisk_baseWidgetData}}\nHigh amount within the category: {{$context.$variables.highCategoryAmountRiskWidgetData}}\nHigh-value vague description risk: {{$context.$variables.highValueVagueDescRiskWidgetData}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1778111033846_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
